comments.body:
@Joe Walker Those comments were very often nasty towards artists, especially female ones. I once collaborated with a BV contributor for another media outlet to cover a new act that involved a well established talent. Once that artist learned BV was also intended to feature this content they demanded it not be placed there. This was specifically because of their negative experience of the comments. 

Let me be the one to say shame on the NYT for not licensing any images from Amanda Hatfield or from BV's pre acquisition heyday.

And negative opinions in this story aside, Bill's writing specifically kept fans like me coming back to this website even when it became overrun with junky looking ads. These people always deserved better. Sad that this is how they will it.
